course: dictionary
lesson: 7767
title: Pursuit: being chased, aiming for, or a hobby
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A pursuit is what happens when someone goes after something. The word has three everyday meanings: chasing someone to catch them, trying hard to get or reach something, and an activity you do for fun. Read the words around it to find which meaning fits.
explain: In the story, Toad «had taken by-paths, and crossed many fields, and changed his course several times, in case of pursuit». The clues are by-paths and changed his course. Toad was dodging someone who was chasing him, so pursuit means being chased.
explain: Now try the other meanings in the same spot. «The pursuit of happiness» means trying to reach happiness, and «outdoor pursuits» means hobbies like sailing and camping. Swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Maths uses the idea too. A dog runs at 8 metres each second after a cat that runs at 6 metres each second, and the cat starts 20 metres ahead. The gap closes by 2 metres every second, so the dog catches the cat in 10 seconds.
fact: Pursuit is a noun, and its plural is pursuits.
fact: Pursuit can mean chasing someone or something to catch them, as in «in pursuit of the thief».
fact: Pursuit can also mean trying hard to get or reach something, as in «the pursuit of knowledge».
fact: A pursuit can be a hobby or activity, as in «outdoor pursuits» like hiking and climbing.
fact: Useful phrases are «in pursuit of», «hot pursuit» (a close chase straight after someone), and «outdoor pursuits».
exercise: In the story Toad changes his course «in case of pursuit». What does pursuit mean here? | *Being chased | A favourite hobby | A long, quiet walk
exercise: The police were «in pursuit of the thief». What does in pursuit of mean? | Painting a picture of the thief | Running away from the thief | Waiting for the thief to come home | *Chasing the thief to catch him
exercise: Which sentence uses pursuit to mean a hobby or activity? | *«She loves her outdoor pursuits, like sailing and camping.» | «He was in hot pursuit down the road.» | «The pursuit of the fox ended at the river.» | «The chase went on for three miles.»
test: A cat runs at 6 m/s and a dog runs at 8 m/s after it. Each second, how much does the gap close by? | 8 metres | *2 metres | 6 metres | 14 metres
test: In «the pursuit of happiness», what is pursuit closest to? | Ending | *Trying hard to reach or get | A hobby or game | Being chased
exam: The explorer spent ten years in pursuit of a lost city. What does pursuit mean here? | A hobby he enjoyed at weekends | Being chased by a city guard | *Trying hard to reach or find | Sleeping on a boat
